                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2b0dee2b-f1f2-3dde-9868-acd835c8924f",
                        "entry_id": "5010a6bb-40ab-38b2-89c2-bf343877c14a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Midday, noon."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cbfbe5ca-7823-457e-8a49-a57d991f3c7b",
                                "sense_id": "2b0dee2b-f1f2-3dde-9868-acd835c8924f",
                                "text": "Quantities and frequencies are distributed as follows (neglecting the meridiem hour):[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "497b3a5d-5b53-446c-bcc8-d294e78ffbb3",
                                "sense_id": "2b0dee2b-f1f2-3dde-9868-acd835c8924f",
                                "text": "The same female number 1 introduced inside the ice-box at 9 a.m., to 9:15 was in lethargy, pick up and put it inside the stove to 350 degrees, to 12 meridiem, was in excellent conditions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82246779-cfb3-4a40-aba2-29a80adf340d",
                                "sense_id": "2b0dee2b-f1f2-3dde-9868-acd835c8924f",
                                "text": "I wrote that the habit of schedulers in the railroad business of skipping the meridiem (they go from 11:59 a.m. to 12:01 p.m. in a split second) “. . . begs the question of what to designate the mass transit of the meridiem.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b6ab3af-1790-40d5-a64a-f5a07fd2df14",
                                "sense_id": "2b0dee2b-f1f2-3dde-9868-acd835c8924f",
                                "text": "But when the sky had brightened for the meridiem—the two to three hours of dull yet hazardous sunlight that filtered through the thick cloud cover each planetary rotation—she’d had to retire underground, losing time."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2cbe5af9-1c67-4610-984f-35f7256dda08",
                                "sense_id": "2b0dee2b-f1f2-3dde-9868-acd835c8924f",
                                "text": "From prior to first light to the meridiem – yes, that means noon – the activities around Leelanau are as varied as the people who call it home:"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "db6d1308-c122-314b-a43c-8a7b5e0365ce",
                        "entry_id": "5010a6bb-40ab-38b2-89c2-bf343877c14a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The property of a timestamp of being either a.m. or p.m."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "33fa0c28-8135-47cd-9667-5cf73923d581",
                                "sense_id": "db6d1308-c122-314b-a43c-8a7b5e0365ce",
                                "text": "The terminal responds N HH MM CR where N, HH, and MM are the meridiem, hour, and minutes, as above."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ceddad3-02e0-4eb6-9196-a2260cbd7c79",
                                "sense_id": "db6d1308-c122-314b-a43c-8a7b5e0365ce",
                                "text": "If a 12-hour clock is specified, the eighth field (the meridiem indicator) is required.[…]If this input string is entered, the parse still recognizes “feb” as the month name and “am” as the meridiem indicator, even though the format string specified both of these fields as uppercase, and the month name as unabbreviated."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0868c92-64f4-421b-9539-4eed19627168",
                                "sense_id": "db6d1308-c122-314b-a43c-8a7b5e0365ce",
                                "text": "if (hour < 12) { meridiem = 'am'; } else { meridiem = 'pm'; }"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e62a4ef8-3ab3-4a0e-a74b-83a38ba72265",
                                "sense_id": "db6d1308-c122-314b-a43c-8a7b5e0365ce",
                                "text": "To the right of the radio buttons, complete the Start Time and End Time fields and select the meridiem from the AM/PM menu to define the time during which the schedule is in effect."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a9d1f82-b37d-4be3-b644-81288de977da",
                                "sense_id": "db6d1308-c122-314b-a43c-8a7b5e0365ce",
                                "text": "Ensure the meridiem (AM/PM) specification is set accordingly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "54421560-2ffc-4578-8a87-6e0cc532eecf",
                                "sense_id": "db6d1308-c122-314b-a43c-8a7b5e0365ce",
                                "text": "Finally, we’ll write the method to render the appointment slot radio buttons. To do this we first have to filter the slots by availabity and by whether AM or PM is selected. Both are simple checks; for the first we see if it exists in state.schedule, for the later, we check the meridiem part with moment().format('a')."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48809572-0a53-4899-8978-242017625fd7",
                                "sense_id": "db6d1308-c122-314b-a43c-8a7b5e0365ce",
                                "text": "The meridiem for a DateTime can be accessed by the \"a\" format token: DateTime.local().setZone(z).toFormat(\"a\") //=> \"PM\" The Luxon Info methods are for finding out what the meridiems are called in different human languages."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "32ecb478-0b48-4c7d-bfbe-5884894f0b8e",
                                "sense_id": "db6d1308-c122-314b-a43c-8a7b5e0365ce",
                                "text": "The digital clock has four parts: hour, minute, second, and meridiem.[…]Assigning the Current Meridiem (AM/PM) / Since the Digital Clock is in a 12-hour format, you need to assign the appropriate meridiem according to the current hour."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
